<h3>Training and inference scaling</h3>
<p>During training, S is sampled uniformly from &#123;1, …, S<sub>max</sub>&#125;. This stochastic schedule forces the shared block to produce coherent representations at any loop depth — including values beyond S<sub>max</sub> at inference time. The training FLOPs scale as:</p>

<div class="math-block">
  <div class="math-label">LoopMDM Training Cost</div>
  F<sub>loop</sub> = F<sub>base</sub> + (E[S] − 1) · n<sub>m</sub> · F<sub>layer</sub><br>
  where E[S] = (S<sub>max</sub> + 1) / 2   <span class="math-comment">← stochastic uniform sampling</span>
</div>

<p>Under matched total training FLOPs (i.e., fewer steps to compensate for per-step cost), LoopMDM reaches the same test NLL as a non-looped baseline with <strong>3.34×</strong> fewer training FLOPs on LM1B and <strong>2.95×</strong> fewer on OpenWebText. At inference time, increasing S improves GSM8K accuracy monotonically — the model even generalizes to S values beyond S<sub>max</sub>.</p>

<table class="results-table" style="margin-top:1rem">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Loop count S</th>
      <th>Gen. Perplexity ↓ (512 steps)</th>
      <th>BoolQ ↑</th>
      <th>RACE ↑</th>
      <th>Avg. (9 tasks) ↑</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>MDM baseline (no loops)</td>
      <td class="mn">55.50</td>
      <td class="mn">46.6</td>
      <td class="mn">28.5</td>
      <td class="mn">40.0</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>LoopMDM S=1</td>
      <td class="mn">55.50</td>
      <td class="mn">53.8</td>
      <td class="mn">27.2</td>
      <td class="mn">39.4</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>LoopMDM S=6</td>
      <td class="mn">48.16</td>
      <td class="mn">53.8</td>
      <td class="mn">31.3</td>
      <td class="mn">40.7</td>
    </tr>
    <tr class="highlight-row">
      <td>LoopMDM S=12</td>
      <td class="mn best">48.16</td>
