<p>The key observation: at S=12, generative perplexity improves by <strong>13%</strong> over the baseline (55.50 → 48.16). This isn't just a compression trick — the model genuinely reasons better about globally constrained predictions. Now imagine what this means for a draft model that must propose tokens conditioned on a large target LLM's context.</p>
</section>

<!-- §04 The Proposal -->
<section id="s-proposal" data-code="proposal">
<div class="section-no">04 — The Looped Drafter</div>
<h2>The Proposal: Loop DFlash's Draft Model</h2>
<p>Here's the core idea: replace DFlash's single-pass denoising step with a LoopMDM-style looped block. Instead of generating all γ draft tokens in one pass, the draft model applies a shared mid-block S times, letting the masked positions iteratively refine their predictions before committing.</p>

